# ~/.config/uwsm/env -- sourced by uwsm before Hyprland starts.
#
# POSIX sh, not fish: uwsm sources this with /bin/sh from
# /usr/lib/uwsm/prepare-env.sh, in a shell that has no fish config in sight.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# uwsm runs the compositor as a systemd user unit (wayland-wm@hyprland.service),
# so the session starts with the user manager's PATH -- /usr/bin and friends,
# and nothing else. The PATH you see in a terminal never reaches it: fish builds
# that per terminal, long after Hyprland and Noctalia are running. Measured
# 2026-08-18 off the running session, /proc/<hyprland>/environ and
# /proc/<noctalia>/environ both read:
#
#   PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/lib/jvm/default/bin:...
#
# ~/.local/bin is where install.sh puts the noct-* scripts, and three things
# look them up by bare name:
#
#   launcher providers  20-launcher.toml runs `noct-audio list sinks` and its
#                       siblings through `sh -lc`. A login shell does not
#                       rescue this -- /etc/profile only appends the system
#                       directories, it does not add ~/.local/bin -- so every
#                       /aout /ain /bt /net /power /theme entry comes back
#                       "No results found", which is also exactly what a
#                       provider with nothing to report looks like.
#
#   exec binds          SUPER+SHIFT+G runs `noct-glass cycle`; Hyprland spawns
#                       it with its own environment, so it fails silently and
#                       the glass level simply stops changing.
#
#   the colors_changed  50-glass.toml runs `noct-glass apply` when the palette
#   hook               changes, so without this the glass stops following the
#                       colour scheme too.
#
# PATH is in uwsm's always_export set (Varnames in uwsm's main.py), so what is
# set here is pushed to the systemd user manager and inherited by every unit
# under it, the compositor included.
#
# This is startup-only. Changing it needs a new session, not a reload: Hyprland
# and Noctalia keep the environment they were spawned with.

# Idempotent because the file is cheap to source twice and a doubled PATH entry
# is the kind of thing nobody notices until they are debugging something else.
case ":$PATH:" in
    *":$HOME/.local/bin:"*) ;;
    *) PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH" ;;
esac
export PATH
